                <pb facs="0153" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg97"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>The Cabinet Committee on Germany (i.e., Hull, Hopkins, Stimson, and Morgenthau)
                    held its first meeting in Hull’s office on the morning of September 5, 1944. The
                    paper entitled “Suggested Recommendations on Treatment of Germany From the
                    Cabinet Committee for the President”, September 4, 1944, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg95">p. 95</ref>, was presented at this meeting.
                        <pb facs="0154" n="98" xml:id="pg98"/> No official minutes of the meeting
                    have been found, but information on the meeting is included in Hull, pp.
                    1608–1609; Stimson and Bundy, pp. 569–570; Morgenthau material printed in Blum,
                    pp. 359–360, and <hi rendition="#italic">Morgenthau Diary</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Germany</hi>), vol. I, pp. 524–528; and <ref
                        target="frus:frus1945Malta/pg_161"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Malta and Yalta, 1945, p.
                    161</ref>.</p>
            </div>
